# hsk apps UI (window.ui → window.py)

When changing the Qt UI of an app under `src/harrix_swiss_knife/apps/`:

1. Edit only the corresponding `window.ui` file.
2. Regenerate `window.py` with `pyside6-uic` (do not hand-edit `window.py`).
3. Wire behavior in `main.py` and other app modules as needed.

Never invent or patch layout/widgets directly in `window.py` — it is generated output.

## Commands (from repo root)

```text
pyside6-uic src/harrix_swiss_knife/apps/fitness/window.ui -o src/harrix_swiss_knife/apps/fitness/window.py
pyside6-uic src/harrix_swiss_knife/apps/finance/window.ui -o src/harrix_swiss_knife/apps/finance/window.py
pyside6-uic src/harrix_swiss_knife/apps/food/window.ui -o src/harrix_swiss_knife/apps/food/window.py
pyside6-uic src/harrix_swiss_knife/apps/habits/window.ui -o src/harrix_swiss_knife/apps/habits/window.py
```

Run the command for the app you changed. Activate the project virtualenv before calling `pyside6-uic`.
